@sikorski_freeze_movements_2026
title: Build one movements council without taking it over
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Join unions, equality groups and the Women's Strike while preserving their autonomy.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Lewica cannot staff a permanent movements secretariat.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; sikorski_protest_strength += 10; movement_autonomy += 4; local_network += 3; party_unity += 1; news_headline = "The repeal protests acquire a common council outside party control"

We convene it and then, deliberately, do not chair it. Unions, equality
organisations and the Women's Strike each keep their own decisions; what the
council provides is a room, a rota of lawyers and one shared calendar so that
three separate protests stop being scheduled on the same afternoon.

It is administratively dull and it is the difference between a season of
overlapping demonstrations and a coalition. Our own press office would prefer
something with a stage and a leader.

- @poland_event_queue: Book the room

@sikorski_freeze_courts_2026
title: Challenge every administrative freeze in court
subtitle: Preserve the line between a hostile ministry and a repealed statute.
on-arrival: sikorski_legal_defence = 1; constitutional_restraint += 4; judicial_legitimacy += 3; sikorski_protest_strength += 4; media_capacity -= 1; news_headline = "Lewica turns the implementation freeze into a chain of reviewable decisions"

Every freeze is challenged separately: the withheld implementation funds, the
suspended inspection powers, the guidance the equality administration stopped
issuing. Each filing makes the same argument — that a ministry which lost the
vote may not repeal a statute by declining to fund it.

The cases are slow and several will be lost. What they establish, while the
repeal bills are still being drafted, is that the government is acting outside
the law rather than merely against our preferences, and that somebody is
keeping the record.

- @poland_event_queue: File the challenges

@sikorski_freeze_strike_2026
title: Call a national social strike
subtitle: Escalate before the repeal bills reach the Sejm and accept an earlier security response.
on-arrival: sikorski_protest_strength += 15; workers_support += 5; labor_credibility += 3; public_trust -= 2; sikorski_police_militarisation += 1; news_headline = "A national social strike meets the cabinet before its repeal bills"

We call it before the bills reach the chamber, on the grounds that a freeze is
already a repeal and waiting for the vote concedes the argument. The public
hospitals and the transport unions come out first; the inspection service,
which has been told its powers are under review, comes out with them.

The escalation is real and so is the answer to it. The Interior Ministry now
has a reason to deploy in February that it would otherwise have had to invent
in April, and every subsequent confrontation begins from a harder position on
both sides.

- @poland_event_queue: Call the date
